<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2016/Discovery-Park-040716.jpg" alt="Plein air painting done at Discovery Park" width="550" height="276" data-filename="Discovery Park 040716.JPG" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Field Study: Discovery Park 040716. 6x12, oil on canvas panel. 2016.</p>
<p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</p>
<div style="text-align: left;">Moving from the Virginia countryside the city of Seattle has forced me to take on a different type of landscape in my paintings; I spent much of the winter trying to paint gray seascapes. However, in Discovery Park there is a small slice of a familiar environment. One of the challenges of painting there is that there are great views everywhere you go. It took a long time for me to pick a setting from all the choices available.</div>
<div style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">&nbsp;</span></div>
<div style="text-align: left;"><span style="line-height: 1.42857;">The sky was clear and the light overall had an orange cast. To avoid painting something that was too yellow, I compensated by sticking to a limited palette of chromatic black, burnt sienna and cad yellow light.</span></div>
<div style="text-align: left;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="text-align: left;">It turned out to be colder than I expected so I did most of the work on location then brought the painting back to the studio to finish it.</div>
<p>&nbsp;</p>